WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.997
Welcome back to Nabulines Academy.

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:03.901
You've built a following.

3
00:00:04.249 --> 00:00:05.341
Ten thousand people.

4
00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:06.931
Maybe a hundred thousand.

5
00:00:07.094 --> 00:00:08.162
You post every day.

6
00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:09.822
The likes roll in.

7
00:00:10.461 --> 00:00:12.736
But here's the hard truth — you don't own

8
00:00:12.794 --> 00:00:13.421
any of it.

9
00:00:14.164 --> 00:00:15.847
Today we're talking about the difference

10
00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.543
between being a creator and being a

11
00:00:17.589 --> 00:00:18.065
builder.

12
00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:21.095
And why one path gives you real power,

13
00:00:21.316 --> 00:00:22.941
while the other keeps you renting.

14
00:00:22.941 --> 00:00:24.206
Let's define terms.

15
00:00:24.845 --> 00:00:27.028
A creator makes content on platforms they

16
00:00:27.086 --> 00:00:27.910
don't control.

17
00:00:28.165 --> 00:00:28.897
Instagram.

18
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:29.710
TikTok.

19
00:00:29.965 --> 00:00:30.534
YouTube.

20
00:00:30.824 --> 00:00:32.519
You're creating value, yes.

21
00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:34.888
But the platform owns the relationship

22
00:00:34.922 --> 00:00:35.921
with your audience.

23
00:00:36.327 --> 00:00:37.813
They decide what gets shown.

24
00:00:38.162 --> 00:00:39.438
They change the algorithm.

25
00:00:39.659 --> 00:00:40.913
They can ban you tomorrow.

26
00:00:41.203 --> 00:00:42.724
You're renting space in someone else's

27
00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:43.188
house.

28
00:00:43.595 --> 00:00:44.268
And the rent?

29
00:00:44.558 --> 00:00:47.229
It's your time, your energy, your ideas.

30
00:00:47.229 --> 00:00:48.320
Now meet the builder.

31
00:00:48.611 --> 00:00:50.329
A builder creates things they own.

32
00:00:50.619 --> 00:00:51.292
A website.

33
00:00:51.583 --> 00:00:52.094
An app.

34
00:00:52.384 --> 00:00:52.929
A tool.

35
00:00:53.278 --> 00:00:53.916
A product.

36
00:00:54.659 --> 00:00:56.610
When someone uses what you built, they

37
00:00:56.668 --> 00:00:57.841
come directly to you.

38
00:00:58.479 --> 00:00:59.141
No middleman.

39
00:00:59.547 --> 00:01:01.312
No algorithm deciding if your work is

40
00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:02.217
worthy today.

41
00:01:02.856 --> 00:01:04.377
You control the experience.

42
00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:05.991
You control the relationship.

43
00:01:06.211 --> 00:01:07.163
You own the asset.

44
00:01:07.628 --> 00:01:09.973
And here's the kicker — what you build can

45
00:01:10.031 --> 00:01:11.424
work for you while you sleep.

46
00:01:11.424 --> 00:01:12.457
Let's get concrete.

47
00:01:13.003 --> 00:01:14.501
You're a fitness creator with fifty

48
00:01:14.559 --> 00:01:16.045
thousand Instagram followers.

49
00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:17.241
Impressive.

50
00:01:17.589 --> 00:01:19.377
But Instagram changes the algorithm.

51
00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.652
Your reach drops eighty percent overnight.

52
00:01:22.117 --> 00:01:23.347
Your income vanishes.

53
00:01:23.986 --> 00:01:25.240
Now imagine you're a builder.

54
00:01:25.704 --> 00:01:26.819
You have a fitness app.

55
00:01:27.283 --> 00:01:28.839
Five thousand paying users.

56
00:01:29.477 --> 00:01:31.242
Instagram could disappear tomorrow.

57
00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:32.902
Your business keeps running.

58
00:01:33.773 --> 00:01:34.690
That's the difference.

59
00:01:34.876 --> 00:01:35.770
One is fragile.

60
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.569
The other is antifragile.

61
00:01:37.569 --> 00:01:39.032
Here's what most people miss.

62
00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.273
Being a builder doesn't mean abandoning

63
00:01:41.331 --> 00:01:42.434
content creation.

64
00:01:43.304 --> 00:01:44.291
The smartest move?

65
00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:45.615
Be both.

66
00:01:46.253 --> 00:01:47.960
Use platforms to reach people.

67
00:01:48.598 --> 00:01:50.456
But drive them to something you own.

68
00:01:50.746 --> 00:01:51.582
Your website.

69
00:01:51.803 --> 00:01:52.801
Your email list.

70
00:01:53.057 --> 00:01:53.684
Your app.

71
00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:55.925
Platforms are megaphones.

72
00:01:56.563 --> 00:01:57.132
Use them.

73
00:01:57.422 --> 00:01:59.013
But never make them your foundation.

74
00:01:59.268 --> 00:02:00.696
Build on land you own.

75
00:02:00.696 --> 00:02:02.449
Why does this matter for you right now?

76
00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:04.539
Because you're about to learn to code.

77
00:02:04.945 --> 00:02:07.360
And coding is the ultimate builder skill.

78
00:02:07.906 --> 00:02:09.508
It lets you create things that exist

79
00:02:09.612 --> 00:02:11.157
independent of any platform.

80
00:02:11.505 --> 00:02:12.863
A website that's yours.

81
00:02:13.119 --> 00:02:14.872
A tool that solves a real problem.

82
00:02:15.162 --> 00:02:16.474
An asset that compounds.

83
00:02:16.695 --> 00:02:18.320
You're not learning to code to get a job.

84
00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:20.341
You're learning to code to own your work.

85
00:02:20.341 --> 00:02:21.804
So here's your exercise.

86
00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:25.008
List one thing you currently rent — a

87
00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:26.227
platform where you're building an

88
00:02:26.274 --> 00:02:26.889
audience.

89
00:02:27.528 --> 00:02:29.745
Then list one thing you could own instead.

90
00:02:30.384 --> 00:02:31.823
Maybe it's a simple website.

91
00:02:32.566 --> 00:02:33.809
Maybe it's an email list.

92
00:02:34.552 --> 00:02:36.375
Maybe it's a tool you wish existed.

93
00:02:37.013 --> 00:02:37.989
Don't overthink it.

94
00:02:38.093 --> 00:02:39.103
Just write it down.

95
00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:41.135
Next lesson, we're diving into the

96
00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:43.457
Nabulines method — how we're going to turn

97
00:02:43.503 --> 00:02:44.885
you from creator into builder in the

98
00:02:44.943 --> 00:02:46.139
fastest way possible.

99
00:02:46.684 --> 00:02:47.509
See you there.
